import json,pathlib,random
R=pathlib.Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1];N={n['id']:n for n in json.loads((R/'data/notes.json').read_text())}
a='''1~The November Q2 GDP estimate measures:~Real July–September year-on-year growth at a stated historical base.~Full-year nominal growth.|The December annual growth forecast.|Identical growth in every sector.
2~Withdrawal of selected QCOs means:~Product-specific mandatory conformity requirements changed.~All BIS standards disappeared.|All products became exempt from every safety law.|Every change was a permanent economy-wide repeal.
3~Which Labour Code chronology is correct?~November commencement, with detailed rule-making and transition still relevant.~All Codes remained only draft Bills.|Every worker received every benefit on commencement day.|All central and state rules were finalised years earlier.
4~Under the EPF enrolment window ₹100 represents:~Specified damages, not the total employer contribution liability.~Waiver of every past employer obligation.|A universal monthly benefit to all workers.|The value of all interest and administrative charges combined.
5~Site-specific oil-mine emergency plans differ from:~A generic checklist proving every hazard is controlled.~Risk assessment.|Contractor training.|Planning for toxic-gas hazards.
6~Notification of DPDP Rules means:~Different provisions may have different commencement timelines.~Every processing duty became immediately operative.|Every rule was deferred identically.|The parent Act was repealed.
7~Parental verification exceptions for specified institutions imply:~Purpose-limited exceptions, not unrestricted commercial reuse.~All education data is exempt from every duty.|Healthcare status permits unlimited resale.|A token gives consent for every later purpose.
8~Which Export Promotion Mission pairing is correct?~Protsahan—trade finance; Disha—non-financial readiness.~Disha—only monetary policy; Protsahan—only heritage.|Both are direct equal cash payments to all citizens.|The entire outlay was already disbursed at approval.
9~The 6,000 MTPA REPM target refers to:~Planned annual integrated magnet capacity.~Mineral reserves already mined.|Output already produced on Cabinet approval day.|A monthly cash payment to every manufacturer.
10~A processed product using a GI ingredient:~Does not automatically gain GI-logo entitlement under the discussed draft.~Always inherits the logo without conditions.|Can ignore product standards.|Automatically becomes a new registered GI.
11~Israel FTA terms of reference are:~A negotiation milestone distinct from September’s investment treaty.~Proof all tariffs were abolished.|The same instrument as every investment agreement.|Evidence the FTA was already in force.
12~An export-credit moratorium is:~A conditional pause in payments, not automatic debt cancellation.~An unconditional principal write-off.|A universal grant to every exporter.|An abolition of all foreign-exchange reporting.
13~The November assent-reference opinion should be read as:~Rejecting court-prescribed universal timelines while allowing limited directions for prolonged inaction.~Endorsing deemed assent as a universal rule.|Removing every possible response to indefinite inactivity.|Keeping April’s timeline position wholly unchanged.
14~A direction to establish a Tribunals Commission proves:~A judicial direction, not actual operational establishment.~Every tribunal was abolished.|The new commission was functioning immediately.|Executive control over adjudication became unrestricted.
15~The retrospective-EC review does not imply:~An unrestricted prospective licence for future violations.~A changed position from the earlier May ruling.|A need to preserve legal chronology.|The relevance of the 2017 cut-off.
16~The draft Seeds Bill must be distinguished from:~An already enacted replacement and a ban on all traditional seed exchange.~A consultation proposal.|Quality regulation.|A traceability framework.
17~A new PLI application round is not necessarily:~A fresh independent budget to add mechanically to every earlier headline.~A policy-stage development.|Subject to product eligibility.|Linked to verified performance.
18~DRDO–DGA cooperation establishes:~A framework, not automatic delivery of every technology.~Unlimited ownership of all French defence IP.|A completed procurement of every listed platform.|Guaranteed local absorption without skills.
19~The revised thermal co-firing policy:~Has differentiated NCR and non-NCR blend requirements.~Makes every coal plant wholly renewable.|Mandates the identical NCR blend everywhere.|Eliminates all combustion emissions.
20~The legal-aid anniversary distinguishes:~1987 enactment from 1995 implementation.~1995 enactment from 1987 implementation.|Eligibility only for convicted people.|Only income-based eligibility with no statutory categories.
21~A G20 voluntary minerals framework is:~Political cooperation, not automatically binding domestic law.~A supranational mining statute.|A guarantee every announced investment occurred.|A replacement for all national mining permissions.
22~COP30’s adaptation-finance signal should not be called:~Money already paid under an automatically binding commitment.~A political direction for scaling finance.|Part of an implementation debate.|Relevant to vulnerable communities.
23~One Health links:~Human, animal and environmental systems.~Only human hospitals.|Only veterinary exports.|A claim every mission stage originated in November.
24~Antimicrobial resistance means:~Microorganisms resist treatment, not that a person becomes immune to antibiotics.~The human body becomes immune to every drug.|Only hospitals can contribute to resistance.|Appropriate treatment should always be denied.
25~Birsa Munda’s November 2025 commemoration concerns:~His 150th birth anniversary.~The 150th anniversary of every tribal rebellion.|His birth in an AP tribal community.|His death in 1875.
26~A brain–computer interface should not be assumed to provide:~Infallible unrestricted access to every private thought.~Task-specific neural-signal interpretation.|Potential therapeutic assistance.|Sensitive-data governance challenges.
27~Farmers’ seed rights under PPV&FR do not imply:~Unrestricted branded commercial sale of every protected variety.~An interest in seed conservation.|A sui generis rights framework.|A balance with breeders’ interests.
28~The CII summit’s MoU totals represent:~Reported proposals, not audited realised spending.~Full money already spent.|Verified net jobs already created.|Amounts necessarily additional to every earlier announcement.
29~A plan for 175 AP MSME parks establishes:~A geographic ambition, not proof all parks are operational.~A finished viable park in every constituency.|Identical jobs in every constituency.|No need for market and infrastructure assessment.
30~A parliamentary committee’s work programme is:~An agenda for examination, not a report of findings.~A completed audit conclusion.|A binding law amending every scheme.|Proof the government accepted unissued recommendations.'''
b='''1~December’s move from 5.5% to 5.25% is:~A 25-basis-point cut.~A 25% rate cut.|A 2.5-percentage-point cut.|A measured full-year GDP outcome.
2~The later Q1 current-account comparator requires:~Preserving release vintages and identifying the revision.~Silently presenting both estimates as final simultaneously.|Calling a deficit a merchandise surplus.|Treating publication month as the reference quarter.
3~IIP differs from GDP because:~It is a covered-industries production index, not whole-economy value added.~It measures all services directly.|Its growth equals every sector’s growth.|It is identical to nominal GDP.
4~An NSC statutory-autonomy recommendation:~Does not itself enact statutory autonomy.~Automatically creates a new Act.|Immediately replaces ISI.|Abolishes the need for transparent methods.
5~SHANTI’s passage should be distinguished from:~Licensing and commissioning actual private nuclear plants.~A legislative milestone.|A framework concerning safety regulation.|A framework concerning liability.
6~Removal of one supplier-recourse ground means:~Neither all operator liability nor all possible recourse necessarily disappears.~Victims can never receive compensation.|Every contractual remedy is abolished.|All nuclear safety obligations end.
7~Under the reviewed Petroleum Rules:~Onshore and offshore granting jurisdictions differ.~Every offshore lease is issued by any state.|A lease waives every environmental approval.|Geological storage needs no authorisation.
8~A VPPA is principally:~A financial contract with renewable-attribute transfer, not physical supply between its parties.~A freely transferable ordinary spot commodity.|A private-wire electricity exchange by definition.|A guarantee price risk disappears.
9~Solar module assembly is not identical to:~Domestic upstream polysilicon, ingot and wafer capability.~An industrial activity.|A potential value-chain stage.|An area for policy evaluation.
10~Electrification audit success requires more than:~Counting connections without service-quality checks.~Verified beneficiary lists.|Sound field surveys.|Inspection follow-through.
11~The reviewed 125-day rural guarantee is:~Per rural household, not an automatic individual salary.~Per person regardless of work demand.|Already paid to everyone upon passage.|Funded without any state role.
12~A provision allowing a seasonal work pause means:~A defined scheduling power, not necessarily an identical nationwide pause.~An obligatory identical calendar everywhere.|Automatic subtraction of sixty from every entitlement.|No need to consider vulnerable households.
13~A committee proposal for broader Gram Sabha consent:~Must not be represented as an enacted universal amendment.~Immediately changes every acquisition statute.|Makes rehabilitation readiness irrelevant.|Abolishes all public-infrastructure acquisition.
14~A 100% insurance FDI ceiling means:~Permission, not proof every insurer is foreign-owned or every household covered.~Compulsory foreign takeover.|Universal automatic insurance.|Guaranteed lower claims rejection.
15~The Securities Markets Code’s December stage was:~Introduction and committee referral.~Completed implementation and repeal of all predecessor Acts.|A final court ruling.|Automatic removal of intermediary registration.
16~December tobacco excise and pan-masala cess changes:~Need separate legal and commencement checks from GST.~Were one identical GST rate from September.|Can be added mechanically without tax-base checks.|Abolish every other tax.
17~The suggested 51% IBC threshold was:~A Select Committee recommendation, not operative law merely from the report.~Already universal upon publication of the report.|A monetary-policy threshold.|The same as every shareholder vote.
18~The VBSA proposal separates:~Higher-education regulation from institutional grant allocation.~Every function into one unchanged UGC office.|Final enactment from no legislative process.|Funding and regulation as necessarily identical.
19~The education-loan report should not be treated as:~An automatic universal debt waiver or operative moratorium change.~A committee recommendation.|An access-to-finance discussion.|Evidence for further policy scrutiny.
20~A Russia urea-project MoU is:~A cooperation milestone, not a factory already producing.~Proof all fertiliser dependence ended.|An unconditional worker-placement guarantee.|A completed project by definition.
21~Tariff-line share differs from import-value share because:~Product classifications and actual trade values have different denominators.~They are always numerically identical.|Tariff lines measure only persons.|Import value is the number of chapters in a treaty.
22~The primary India–NZ conclusion announcement is dated:~22 December 2025.~18 December solely because of the PRS reference label.|1 October 2025.|The date of automatic entry into force.
23~December Labour Code draft rules:~Do not become final merely because the parent Codes commenced in November.~Prove the Codes never commenced.|Are final nationwide detail at consultation launch.|Remove the role of state applicability.
24~Draft gig-worker thresholds establish:~Proposed eligibility conditions, not proof benefits were paid.~Universal PF payment to every platform user.|No need for enrolment.|Final implementation of every scheme.
25~The PMKVY placement ratio requires:~Its component and audit-period denominator.~Reading it as the national unemployment rate.|Applying it to every phase and every trainee automatically.|Assuming every placement was sustained high-paid work.
27~Withdrawal of mandatory app pre-installation:~Does not necessarily abolish the underlying service.~Makes the withdrawn mandate permanently operative.|Proves every installation is compulsory.|Removes all privacy questions.
28~PESA principally concerns:~Fifth Schedule Areas with Part IX modifications.~Every square kilometre of AP uniformly.|Only Sixth Schedule councils.|An identical absolute veto in every consultation provision.
30~Groundwater stage of extraction uses:~Extraction divided by annual extractable resources.~Extraction divided by total recharge in all cases.|Rainfall divided by population.|National average as proof every block is safe.
34~Deepavali’s UNESCO recognition is:~Living heritage on the Representative List, not a new World Heritage monument.~A physical World Heritage site by definition.|An exemption from environmental rules.|Ownership monopoly over every celebration.
35~The final reported AP arrangement adds:~Markapuram and Polavaram; Madanapalle becomes Annamayya headquarters.~Three districts taking the total to twenty-nine.|A separate third district solely from a headquarters shift.|Only a new revenue division with no districts.'''
for mm,name,rows in [('11','November',a),('12','December',b)]:
 Q=[]
 for line in rows.splitlines():
  idx,text,correct,wrong=line.split('~');ref='E7-25'+mm+'-'+idx.zfill(3);ref='CA-035' if ref=='E7-2511-008' else ref;n=N[ref];opts=[correct]+wrong.split('|');random.Random(ref).shuffle(opts)
  Q.append(dict(id=name[:3].upper()+f'-{len(Q)+1:02}',question=text,options=opts,answer=opts.index(correct),explanation=n['static_link']+' '+n['analysis'][0]+' Caution: '+n['trap'],ref=ref))
 assert len(Q)==30
 (R/'data'/f'{name.lower()}-mcqs.json').write_text(json.dumps(Q,ensure_ascii=False,indent=2)+'\n')
# Bespoke implementation lenses supplement each dated note's original analytical material.
F={
'11':[(3,'State rules, worker awareness, inspection and accessible remedies','Coverage and timely benefits, disaggregated by employment type'),(6,'Consent interfaces, records, breach response and independent grievance handling','Comprehension, withdrawal completion and remedy time'),(8,'Affordable finance alongside testing, standards and logistics','First-time exporter retention and verified orders, not only applications'),(9,'Oxide-to-metal processing, alloys, magnet quality and skilled supply chains','Commissioned qualified output and import dependence at each stage'),(13,'Constitutional limits, dialogue and reasons for prolonged inaction','Whether constitutional functions are discharged without judicial substitution'),(15,'Exceptional legacy treatment with appraisal, remediation and deterrent costs','Remediation delivered and prevention of subsequent violations'),(22,'Finance access, adaptation evidence and support for transition-dependent communities','Disbursed accessible finance and locally verified resilience outcomes'),(28,'Project dashboards distinguishing MoU, closure, construction and operation','Incremental investment and net sustained jobs with regional distribution')],
'12':[(5,'Independent safety capability, licensing capacity and transparent compensation','Operational safety, emergency readiness and timely victim compensation'),(11,'Demand capture, fiscal sharing, wage payments and state contingency planning','Timely work/payment and enforceable unemployment allowance'),(13,'Understandable consultation and service-ready rehabilitation before possession','Restored livelihoods, tenure security and functioning local services'),(14,'Capital and competition with solvency, claims and consumer protection','Coverage depth and claim resolution rather than ownership alone'),(18,'Clear regulator/funder boundaries and fair institutional due process','Quality, access and autonomy, not only compliance filings'),(25,'District skill-demand studies, credible assessment and employer feedback','Retention and earnings after placement, independently sampled'),(30,'Aquifer/mandal water budgets, recharge and demand-side crop choices','Seasonal levels and quality alongside transparent extractable-resource estimates'),(35,'Gazette-verified boundaries, transition staffing and citizen-facing service continuity','Travel/access time, workload and grievance resolution rather than district count')]}
for mm,name in [('11','November'),('12','December')]:
 lines=['# '+name+' 2025 · Eight original Mains frameworks','','Original planning aids, not official answers or predicted questions. Evidence is dated; recommendations below are analytical guidance.']
 for idx,design,metric in F[mm]:
  ref='E7-25'+mm+'-'+str(idx).zfill(3);n=N['CA-035' if ref=='E7-2511-008' else ref]
  lines+=['','## '+n['mains'],'','**Study reference:** '+n['id'],'','**Opening distinction:** '+n['static_link'],'','**Dated anchor:** '+n['facts'][0]+' '+n['facts'][1],'','**Argument:** '+n['analysis'][0],'','**Counterargument / limit:** '+n['trap'],'','**Implementation priorities:** '+design+'.','', '**Evaluation:** '+metric+'.','', '**AP / linkage angle:** '+n['analysis'][1],'','**Suggested 150–250-word structure:** Define the mechanism in two sentences; cite the dated anchor; develop two benefits and two constraints; propose the priorities above with a responsible institution; conclude using the evaluation criterion rather than another announcement.']
 (R/'volumes'/f'{name}-2025-Mains-Frameworks.md').write_text('\n'.join(lines)+'\n')
print('Created 60 MCQs and 16 tailored Mains plans')
